<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-23wlw census follow-up (2026-07-26) — the catalog-side twin of
    memory-002's diacritic folding.

    THE GAP. catalog-015 fixed catalog_documents' SEPARATOR half in 2026-07-13
    (nexus-8gue1, GH #1397) and stopped there. Nothing in the expression folds
    diacritics, so the catalog diverges from the SQLite FTS5 baseline exactly
    the way nexus.memory did:

        column   content        query      sqlite  service
        author   Kurt Gödel     Godel           1        0
        author   Müller         Muller          1        0
        author   Schröder       Schroder        1        0

    This is the THIRD time this parity claim has been falsified, and the
    second time on THIS table. catalog-015's own comment recorded that
    catalog-001's "PG >= FTS5 superset" claim was false for filenames; it is
    also false for diacritics, and fixing only the half that had been reported
    is what left this behind.

    WHY author IS THE FIELD THAT MATTERS. Academic author names are where
    diacritics actually live. Measured against the LIVE catalog rather than
    assumed — 51 sampled papers, 5 with non-ASCII authors:

        Sven Groß, Arnold Reusken               ß      NOT a divergence
        Ángel Plaza, Maŕıa-Cecilia Rivara       Á      DIVERGENCE
        Jan Brandts, Sergey Korotov, M. Křížek  ř í ž  NOT a divergence
        Sergey Korotov, Michal Křížek           ř í ž  NOT a divergence
        Miroslav S. Petrov, Тодор Д. Тодоров    Cyril  NOT a divergence

    Only ONE genuinely diverges: searching 'Angel' finds 'Ángel Plaza' under
    FTS5 and returns nothing here. The other four are unfolded by BOTH
    substrates — ß is not expanded, Latin Extended-A (Křížek) and Cyrillic are
    outside FTS5's default remove_diacritics=1 range — so they agree already.
    Stating that plainly because the raw "5 of 51 have non-ASCII authors"
    number overstates the defect by 5x; the real incidence in the sample is
    1 in 51.

    SCOPE. Folding wraps EVERY segment, not just author: title carries
    diacritics at least as often as author does (a paper's title repeats the
    accented terms of its field), and file_path can too. Cheap to include
    because replace-not-add is index-size-neutral. The separator segment keeps
    its existing title+file_path scope — no new evidence widened it, and
    catalog-015's reasoning for that scope still holds.

    fold_diacritics is created by memory-002-0, which this changeset is
    ordered after in db.changelog-master.xml. It is a 1:1 translate() over the
    Latin-1 supplement, chosen over the unaccent extension because unaccent is
    absent from every shipped PG bundle (CREATE EXTENSION aborts Liquibase at
    boot) and because it folds Latin-Ext-A/Greek/Cyrillic that FTS5 leaves
    alone — see memory-002's comment for the full measurement.

    QUERY SIDE. CatalogRepository.searchDocuments applies the identical fold.
    Both halves are required: the stored lexemes are folded, so an unfolded
    query leg stops matching accented input that matched before.

    MECHANICS. PG cannot ALTER a generated column's expression: DROP + re-ADD
    (table rewrite) + recreate the GIN index. Same ACCESS EXCLUSIVE framing as
    catalog-014/-015 — nothing serves during the single-instance rm-then-run
    boot window — and Liquibase runs the changeset in one transaction, so an
    interrupted rewrite rolls back whole rather than leaving a dropped-column
    limbo. DDL only, no row DML, so the FORCE-RLS silent-no-op class
    (nexus-1wjmq) does not apply.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="catalog-017-0" author="nexus-23wlw">
        <comment>catalog_documents.fts_vector: fold Latin-1 diacritics on every segment so 'Godel' finds 'Gödel' (the half catalog-015 left behind)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true">
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_catalog_documents_fts;
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_documents DROP COLUMN fts_vector;
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_documents
    ADD COLUMN fts_vector tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS (
        to_tsvector('english', nexus.fold_diacritics(coalesce(title, '')))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  nexus.fold_diacritics(coalesce(author, '')))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  nexus.fold_diacritics(coalesce(corpus, '')))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  nexus.fold_diacritics(coalesce(file_path, '')))
        || to_tsvector('simple',
               nexus.fold_diacritics(
                   translate(coalesce(title, '') || ' ' || coalesce(file_path, ''),
                             '/.-_', '    ')))
    ) STORED;
CREATE INDEX idx_catalog_documents_fts
    ON nexus.catalog_documents USING GIN (fts_vector);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_catalog_documents_fts;
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_documents DROP COLUMN fts_vector;
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_documents
    ADD COLUMN fts_vector tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS (
        to_tsvector('english', coalesce(title, ''))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  coalesce(author, ''))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  coalesce(corpus, ''))
        || to_tsvector('simple',  coalesce(file_path, ''))
        || to_tsvector('simple',
               translate(coalesce(title, '') || ' ' || coalesce(file_path, ''),
                         '/.-_', '    '))
    ) STORED;
CREATE INDEX idx_catalog_documents_fts
    ON nexus.catalog_documents USING GIN (fts_vector);
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
